WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:08.680
Since 2014, a working group has been developing
proposals for the rehabilitation of the Kaiapoi River.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:14.180
Today we are opposite the new Coastguard building
just downstream of the Williams Street Bridge.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.920
Now Neville, I must say it looks fabulous
across the river here.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.260
I can see a lot of hard work has gone into
making it look beautiful.

00:00:21.269 --> 00:00:24.310
Can you tell me please what's happening with
water quality here?

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:28.330
Yeah, well right up and down the river with
everything we've talked about so far, is all

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:33.180
about trying to just take small steps to enhance
the water quality.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:38.060
As you know, we've got things flowing into
the water that need to be a lot cleaner than they are.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:42.640
There's influences from upstream, there's
the push-back from the Waimakariri.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:47.860
We need to make sure that every step we take
enhances the water quality of this river.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:52.560
And that's ultimately where we want to go,
we want to make sure that this river is cleaned up.

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:58.980
It is in a shocking state, make no bones about
that, it is absolutely shocking and it needs rehabilitation.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:05.300
Unfortunately, it's the long-game not the
short-game and we have to carry on just doing

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:10.220
step-by-step to make sure we can try to get
some better water quality in here.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.840
Now I understand there's going to be some
dredging taking place, is it just going to

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.880
be here? Or how is that all going to work?

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:24.040
Sure, this is obviously the area that is navigated
by boats in and out of here and where they

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:27.880
will park and where they will leave from or
come to.

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:32.750
So there will be a channel through here, one
of the other sediment traps we talked about

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:36.479
earlier could possibly be the actual wharf
area itself.

00:01:36.479 --> 00:01:40.200
So when it comes to re-dredging again, the
wharf area itself will be one of the main

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.450
dredging points as opposed to dredging the
whole river.

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:48.909
The river deepness past the Courtenay Stream
which is the confluence downstream from here,

00:01:48.909 --> 00:01:53.950
which will also be planted in the manner that
you saw up there on the corner, that will

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:57.630
also play a big part in the navigation through
here.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:01.840
So it will be dredged down to there, the depth
of the water is probably not too bad from

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:05.540
there on in through to the Waimakariri.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:09.560
So how can people have their say?

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:14.440
Well, right here they can come in and there
will be an open day at Ruataniwha and people

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:15.650
can have their input that way.

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:19.930
We have the website, we have councillors,
community board members and we really want

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:21.319
people to have their input.

00:02:21.319 --> 00:02:26.690
There are six proposals we'd like your feedback
on, attend our open day on the 27th of April

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:31.480
or find out more at waimakariri.govt.nz

